@startuml scaling
!theme plain
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 46
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

title What scales horizontally, and what does not

header
<b>A shard key is a design decision, not a deployment one.</b>  Retrofitting one means changing every caller, so each service below
declares its unit now.  <b>Green scales out.  Amber scales out within a bound.  Red does not scale out at all</b> — and the red one is
red because of the wire protocol, not the implementation.
endheader

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "**scales out freely** — stateless over its own store" as FREE #C8E6C9 {
  component "**permissions**\nshard: **stateless**\n—\nACL evaluation walks the tree, and a busy\nchannel produces many identical in-flight\nqueries. **Coalesce them** rather than cache:\na cache needs invalidation, coalescing\ndoes not. «Discord's data-services trick»" as perms #FFFFFF
  component "**userdata** · **text** · **pchat**\n**moderation** · **social** · **audit**\n**push** · **files/http** · **operator-api**\nshard: **stateless**\n—\nHistory-bearing services key rows by\n**UUIDv7**: coordination-free and\ntime-sortable. A central sequence is a\nbottleneck; UUIDv4 destroys index locality." as rest #FFFFFF
}

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "**scales out, bounded by the key**" as BOUND #FFF9C4 {
  component "**gateway**\nshard: **connection**\n—\nAny pod takes any connection. A client's\nTCP socket pins it for that connection's\nlifetime; **RESUME** lets it land elsewhere\nafter a restart." as gw #FFFFFF
  component "**session-lifecycle**\nshard: **connection**\n—\nOne state machine per connection,\nindependent of every other." as slife #FFFFFF
  component "**session-view**\nshard: **session id — from day one**\n—\nHolds a composed view per connected\nsession and updates all of them on every\nchange. Unsharded, that is one actor doing\nevery domain read —\n**Discord's guild-process bottleneck, relocated.**" as sview #FFE082
  component "**metadata** · **server-config**\nshard: **virtual server**\n—\nOne actor per virtual server, the Discord\nguild-process pattern. Within one virtual\nserver it scales **vertically only** — which\nis also the answer to multiple virtual\nservers in one deployment." as meta #FFFFFF
  component "**screenshare**\nshard: **SFU session**\n—\nEach broadcast is independent, and Fancy\nclients learn their SFU endpoint from the\nanswer, so placement is free." as share #FFFFFF
}

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "**does not scale out for legacy clients**" as PINNED #FFCDD2 {
  component "**voice**\nshard: **channel, never client**" as voice #FFFFFF
}

note bottom of PINNED #FFCDD2
  **Audio routing is per channel, so a channel's members must share a pod.**
  Client affinity — `sessionAffinity: ClientIP` — is actively wrong: it scatters
  a channel across pods, and there is **no inter-pod audio path** in this design.
  Discord assigns a voice *channel* to a voice server and **tells** the client
  which one. Mumble has no such field, and
  **a legacy client sends UDP to the port it made TCP to.**
  It cannot be redirected.
  Three ways out, and only the last scales:
  · **one voice pod per virtual server** — vertical only, simplest, honest
  · **a forwarding mesh between voice pods** — scales, costs a hop inside a 10 ms budget
  · **shard by channel and hand Fancy clients an explicit endpoint** in ServerSync —
    real scaling for Fancy, legacy pinned to the advertised pod
end note

note right of sview #FFE082
  **Why this one is amber and not green.**
  10 000 sessions means 10 000 composed views, all
  maintained by one actor. Sharding by session id
  makes it green; not choosing a key now makes it
  the first thing to fall over, and the hardest to
  fix, because every service in the domain calls it.
end note

note bottom of BOUND #FFFFFF
  **Every actor mailbox is bounded and has a shed policy.**
  An unbounded inbox converts one slow consumer into an OOM — the
  specific failure Discord hit with Erlang process mailboxes under
  fanout. Applies to session-view per session and metadata per
  virtual server alike.
end note

note bottom of FREE #FFFFFF
  **Deadlines are not enough on their own.** A saturated service
  makes every caller wait its full deadline and *then* fail, burning
  capacity the whole time. A **circuit breaker** per service plus
  load shedding at the gateway fails fast instead.
end note

legend bottom
|= colour |= meaning |
|<#C8E6C9>   | scales out freely — add pods |
|<#FFF9C4>   | scales out along a declared key |
|<#FFE082>   | scales out **only if** the key is designed in now |
|<#FFCDD2>   | cannot scale out; a protocol limit, not a code one |
endlegend

@enduml
